Jenkins Utility Jobs Overview
This page catalogs self-service Jenkins utility jobs available to all teams. These are shared, general-purpose automations - that anyone can run without needing to request help from an admin.

Who can use these: All project teams. Each utility runs on the requesting team's own dedicated Jenkins agent, so jobs work across different teams' environments as needed.

Who can contribute: Utilities aren't limited to IMAC - any team can add a new one. To contribute a new utility job:

Go to the imac-jenkins-jobs GitHub repo
Add your job definition under the project's JSON job definitions, under the Utility folder
Create a PR for IMAC and post it in this Team's channel for review and approval Pull Requests
Update this confluence page with the Job's usage in the same format as the entries below
GitHub Create New Repo
What it does: Creates a new GitHub repository based on a specified template or existing repo, and applies standard repository settings (branch protection, permissions, etc. — per GitHub Repository Governance). If the repo already exists, no new repo is created — the job simply reapplies those standard settings to it.

Jenkins Job: GitHub Create New Repo

